Adaptation (cmd/fak turnkey up structured carriers): no upstream code is
adapted; the contract is inspired by the finding. Upstream carries so_args on
every request's SamplingParams (sampling_params.py:59,82) and builds the
structured-output matcher at enqueue (llm_engine.py:606-612), while PR#119
drops logprobs without a word (sampling_params.py:63). The fak up turnkey
server had dropped carriers the same silent way: /v1/completions dropped
response_format and all nine guided-decode carriers (guided_json,
guided_regex, guided_choice, guided_grammar, guided_decoding_backend,
json_schema, regex, ebnf, structured_outputs), and /v1/chat/completions,
which already carried response_format, dropped the nine guided carriers. Both
routes now pass the same ten carriers to the planner as fak serve does, and a
native structured-output refusal maps to the gateway's planner-level typed
code (400 native_structured_output_unsupported, 500
native_structured_decode_failed) instead of a plain 500 or a silently
unconstrained 200. The gateway's ingress caps are not reproduced here: a
guided_regex over 4096 bytes gets 400 native_structured_output_unsupported on
fak up but 400 parameter_out_of_range on fak serve, and the 422
invalid_response_format / json_schema_* and 400 invalid_structured_outputs
ingress codes are not emitted. A mid-stream native_structured_decode_failed
still surfaces in-band as inference_error.
